1
00:00:03,856 --> 00:00:06,277
The Lives Of The Prophets Part 1,

2
00:00:06,754 --> 00:00:10,469
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

3
00:00:11,778 --> 00:00:15,919
Abrahim عليه السّلام came to Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل)

4
00:00:16,173 --> 00:00:19,617
by the way, Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) made many visits to Makkah.

5
00:00:20,641 --> 00:00:23,657
One of these visits in a Hadith(حديث) narrated by Bukhari(بخاريْ);

6
00:00:23,687 --> 00:00:29,945
Ibrahim عليه السّلام comes to Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) and tell him, we have been commanded to build the house of Allah.

7
00:00:30,722 --> 00:00:35,513
So Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) started building the house of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

8
00:00:36,878 --> 00:00:44,354
The spot of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), the spot itself is sacred and holy since the earth was created.

9
00:00:45,465 --> 00:00:48,838
It's a sacred land since the time of Adam(آدَم).

10
00:00:50,282 --> 00:00:59,320
And that spot was known and Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) used to make Hajj(حَجْ) to that area, the spot itself.

11
00:01:00,050 --> 00:01:09,408
But there is a dispute and difference among the Ulama(علماء) whether Adam(آدَم) has built anything over there or not.

12
00:01:11,003 --> 00:01:14,076
Most likely, the first one who established the house is Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم).

13
00:01:15,846 --> 00:01:20,485
But the spot itself was holy from before.

14
00:01:20,795 --> 00:01:24,611
It didn't become holy, the moment in which Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)  was built on it.

15
00:01:24,675 --> 00:01:30,389
No! That spot itself is, is holy and sacred, just like Al-Masjid Al-Aqsa(ألمسجد ألأقصي),

16
00:01:30,770 --> 00:01:37,588
when Rasool Allah ﷺ visited the Al-Masjid Al-Aqsa(ألمسجد ألأقصي) in the trip of Al-Isra(ألأسراء), there wasn't anything built there.

17
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:44,131
In fact, when Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) opened Jerusalem it was used as a dumpster there was garbage in that spot.

18
00:01:44,948 --> 00:01:48,632
But still that was Al-Masjid Al-Aqsa(ألمسجد ألأقصي)  that was the holy sacred mosque.

19
00:01:49,417 --> 00:01:59,413
And then the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم and in the time of Abdul Malik Bin Marwan(عبدالملك بن مروان) they built the two mosques that are enclosed in that Haram(حرم),

20
00:01:59,699 --> 00:02:01,612
but before it was a piece of land.

21
00:02:02,421 --> 00:02:05,659
What makes it special, it's a piece of land.?

22
00:02:06,056 --> 00:02:12,477
What makes Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) the land under it special, when it's a desert and nothing grows there.

23
00:02:13,079 --> 00:02:15,208
It's desert what makes it special?

24
00:02:15,851 --> 00:02:17,550
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

25
00:02:17,629 --> 00:02:19,442
يَخْلُقُ مَا يَشَآءُ وَيَخْتَارُ ۗ

26
00:02:19,828 --> 00:02:24,696
Allah  creates everything He wants, and He chooses out of them.

27
00:02:25,268 --> 00:02:30,933
Allah chooses the best, Allah chooses the worst, Allah chooses what is in between, it's up to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

28
00:02:31,354 --> 00:02:35,401
Allah is the One, Who created the days and Allah is the One, Who chose the best of them to be Friday.

29
00:02:36,116 --> 00:02:41,203
Allah is the One, Who created the days of the year and chose Eid- Al-Ad'haa(عيدالأضحى) and Eid-Ul-Fitr(عيدالفطر) to be the best.

30
00:02:41,528 --> 00:02:46,290
Allah created the month and chose Ramadan(رمضان) to be the holy month of fasting.

31
00:02:46,441 --> 00:02:51,778
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is the One, Who created the days and gave the most reward for the 10 days of Dhul-Hijjah(ذوالحجة).

32
00:02:51,897 --> 00:02:56,311
Allah is the One, Who created the nights and Allah has given the special rewards and the nights of Ramadan(رمضان).

33
00:02:56,477 --> 00:03:00,588
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى also created the nights and He has made the special night Lailat-Ul-Qadr(ليلة القدر).

34
00:03:00,763 --> 00:03:05,415
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى created the earth and He chose Makkah and Madina and Bat-Ul-Maqsad(بيت المقدس) to be special.

35
00:03:05,645 --> 00:03:10,724
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is the One, Who created human beings and they chose Muhammadﷺ to be the best among them.

36
00:03:11,867 --> 00:03:13,572
يَخْلُقُ مَا يَشَآءُ وَيَخْتَارُ ۗ

37
00:03:13,881 --> 00:03:17,127
 Allah creates whatever He wants and then He chooses of them.

38
00:03:17,921 --> 00:03:27,087
So that area, it doesn't have to be a certain dimension and certain physical characteristics and certain shape and certain plants for it, to be special.

39
00:03:28,214 --> 00:03:32,453
These are not the conditions and requirements that apply to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى

40
00:03:32,483 --> 00:03:37,638
because Allah is free of all of these rules and regulations, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is the creator.

41
00:03:39,630 --> 00:03:45,856
So that spot was holy sacred from the beginning of the creation of the earth.

42
00:03:47,475 --> 00:03:53,624
Ibrahim عليه السّلام and Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) started building the house, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

43
00:03:54,156 --> 00:04:09,340
وَإِذ يَرفَعُ إِبراهيمُ القَواعِدَ مِنَ البَيتِ وَإِسماعيلُ رَبَّنا تَقَبَّل مِنّا ۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ السَّميعُ العَليمُ۝

44
00:04:09,887 --> 00:04:15,521
And remember when Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and his son Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) were raising the foundations of the house.

45
00:04:16,458 --> 00:04:23,089
 Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and Ismail عليه السّلام, when they were building the house of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى they had Dua(دُعَا).

46
00:04:23,677 --> 00:04:38,456
رَبَّنا وَاجعَلنا مُسلِمَينِ لَكَ وَمِن ذُرِّيَّتِنا أُمَّةً مُسلِمَةً لَكَ وَأَرِنا مَناسِكَنا وَتُب عَلَينا ۖ

47
00:04:39,441 --> 00:04:46,929
وَتُب عَلَينا ۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ التَّوّابُ الرَّحيمُ۝

48
00:04:48,072 --> 00:05:01,062
رَبَّنا وَابعَث فيهِم رَسولًا مِنهُم يَتلو عَلَيهِم آياتِكَ وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ الكِتابَ وَالحِكمَةَ وَيُزَكّيهِم ۚ

49
00:05:02,189 --> 00:05:11,863
وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ الكِتابَ وَالحِكمَةَ وَيُزَكّيهِم ۚ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ العَزيزُ الحَكيمُ۝

50
00:05:12,014 --> 00:05:17,679
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says and remember when Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and his son Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل), were raising the foundations of the house saying;

51
00:05:17,933 --> 00:05:23,600
Our Lord accept the service from us verily You are the All Hearer, the All Knower, O Allah accept this from us.

52
00:05:25,038 --> 00:05:27,942
Our Lord, and make us submissive unto You,

53
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:32,387
and of our offspring and nation submissive unto You,

54
00:05:32,593 --> 00:05:36,513
and show us our Manasic(مناسك), the Hajj(حَجْ), how to do Hajj(حَجْ)?

55
00:05:36,743 --> 00:05:41,013
Our Lord, send amongst them a messenger of their own,

56
00:05:41,372 --> 00:05:49,912
who shall recite unto them Your verses and instruct them in the book and Sanctify them, verily you are Almighty and All Wise.

57
00:05:50,205 --> 00:05:54,448
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل), they asked Allah to accept it from them.

58
00:05:54,741 --> 00:05:58,598
And they asked Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to make them submissive to Allah; Muslimeen(مسلمين)

59
00:05:58,837 --> 00:06:03,668
and they asked Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, to make their descendants submissive to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

60
00:06:03,883 --> 00:06:07,168
And then they asked Allah to send among these people a Nabi(نَبِي).

61
00:06:07,383 --> 00:06:08,550
Who's that Nabi(نَبِي) ?

62
00:06:09,081 --> 00:06:10,315
Muhammadﷺ

63
00:06:10,345 --> 00:06:11,573
Allah accepted the Dua(دُعَا).

64
00:06:11,764 --> 00:06:14,807
They asked Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to give this Nabi(نَبِي) three things.

65
00:06:14,934 --> 00:06:16,316
يَتْلُو عَلَيْهِمْ آيَاتِهِ

66
00:06:16,545 --> 00:06:18,886
He recites unto them Your verses,

67
00:06:19,322 --> 00:06:21,539
وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ الكِتابَ وَالحِكمَةَ

68
00:06:21,761 --> 00:06:24,690
He teaches them, the book and wisdom, what is wisdom?

69
00:06:25,158 --> 00:06:26,555
Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

70
00:06:26,761 --> 00:06:28,203
 وَيُزَكّيهِم

71
00:06:28,853 --> 00:06:30,868
Sanctify them and purify them.

72
00:06:31,265 --> 00:06:35,341
So Muhammadﷺ  purifies us.

73
00:06:35,468 --> 00:06:38,135
Tazkia(تزكية) purifies us.

74
00:06:38,452 --> 00:06:42,680
Following the way of Muhammadﷺ is the purification for us.

75
00:06:43,275 --> 00:06:51,667
Because if you look at the Da'wah(دعوة) of Muhammadﷺ, you see that he has started out with men that had hearts like rock.

76
00:06:54,139 --> 00:06:58,195
And then look at how Rasool Allah ﷺ carried them from this state

77
00:06:58,727 --> 00:07:02,839
and He elevated them to Make them the best generation that lived on the face of the earth.

78
00:07:03,402 --> 00:07:10,311
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى accepted the Dua(دُعَا) of Ibrahim عليه السّلام and sent to this Ummah(امة) Muhammadﷺ.

79
00:07:13,256 --> 00:07:22,259
We'll finish up with the story of Ibrahim عليه السّلام by mentioning some of his qualities.

80
00:07:24,482 --> 00:07:27,254
Ibrahim عليه السّلام is from Ulul Azm-e-Min-Ar-Rusul(اولي العزم من الرسل).

81
00:07:27,284 --> 00:07:30,363
Ulul Azm-e-Min-Ar-Rusul(اولي العزم من الرسل) I can't find an exact translation of it.

82
00:07:30,681 --> 00:07:34,034
But they are five Ulul Azm(اولي العزم) and these are the greatest of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah.

83
00:07:34,064 --> 00:07:39,418
They are five; Muhammadﷺ, Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم), Musa(موسى), Eesa(عيسى) and Nuh(نوح).

84
00:07:40,323 --> 00:07:47,279
And Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) says that the second greatest among them after Muhammadﷺ is Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم).

85
00:07:48,485 --> 00:07:54,459
 Ibrahim عليه السّلام was mentioned the Qur'an about 73 times in 25 places.

86
00:07:56,570 --> 00:08:02,114
Ibrahim عليه السّلام is the one, whom Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has called in Qur'an, Khalil-Ullah(خليل الله).

87
00:08:02,463 --> 00:08:04,415
The friend of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

88
00:08:04,860 --> 00:08:08,407
Allah has chose Ibrahim عليه السّلام to be His friend.

89
00:08:09,495 --> 00:08:11,592
Ibrahim عليه السّلام lived a lonely life.

90
00:08:11,681 --> 00:08:15,103
He would travel from one place to another around the world making Hijrah(هجرة),

91
00:08:15,370 --> 00:08:19,296
he lived in Iraq for a while in Harran(حرَّان), in Bait-Ul-Maqdis(بيت المقدس) in Egypt.

92
00:08:19,326 --> 00:08:20,994
He visited Makkah few times.

93
00:08:21,192 --> 00:08:24,565
All of this is traveling in difficult conditions.

94
00:08:24,787 --> 00:08:29,578
And Ibrahim عليه السّلام was driven out of his homeland, no believers with him except his nephew, Lut(لوط)

95
00:08:29,879 --> 00:08:35,429
and then he went all over these other countries and he didn't have many followers with him.

96
00:08:35,898 --> 00:08:39,263
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) that I am your friend.

97
00:08:40,326 --> 00:08:42,675
You don't need any friends in this world; I'm your friend.

98
00:08:44,525 --> 00:08:51,329
Also, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given Ibrahim عليه السّلام a name that wasn't given to anybody else in Qur'an.

99
00:08:52,079 --> 00:08:54,545
You know, when we're talking about Muhammadﷺ;

100
00:08:54,635 --> 00:09:01,673
 O Muhammadﷺ have patience and stay with the ones, who remember Allah in night and day.

101
00:09:02,165 --> 00:09:05,538
Allah is commanding Muhammadﷺ to stay with the believers.

102
00:09:06,872 --> 00:09:12,151
Nuh(نوح) when his people came and told them leave these weak people alone,

103
00:09:12,317 --> 00:09:14,510
he said: No! These are the believers with me.

104
00:09:14,540 --> 00:09:16,559
I will be with them; I will remain with them.

105
00:09:16,964 --> 00:09:22,520
These Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) they had believers around them; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told them to remain with these believers.

106
00:09:22,758 --> 00:09:23,478
Why?

107
00:09:23,655 --> 00:09:26,448
Because we need to have an environment of Eeman(ايمان).

108
00:09:26,678 --> 00:09:30,329
We need to live in an environment of Eeman(ايمان), we need to have the support around us.

109
00:09:30,620 --> 00:09:32,955
It's difficult for human being to live alone.

110
00:09:33,202 --> 00:09:38,507
We need to have the support and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is commanding Muhammadﷺ to stay with the believers.

111
00:09:38,650 --> 00:09:40,832
Allah commanding Nuh(نوح) to stay with the believers.

112
00:09:41,039 --> 00:09:44,997
We know that Hud(هود) was with the believer; Saleh(صالح) stayed with the believers;

113
00:09:45,027 --> 00:09:47,559
Musa(موسى) stayed with the believers and so on and so forth.

114
00:09:48,916 --> 00:09:50,615
Ibrahim عليه السّلام is different.

115
00:09:50,877 --> 00:09:53,615
First of all, Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) was making Hijrah(هجرة) for his life.

116
00:09:54,837 --> 00:09:58,043
And then in many places he would go; he would be the only believer.

117
00:09:58,140 --> 00:10:01,942
He went to Egypt, he told his wife: Me and you are the only believers here.

118
00:10:02,482 --> 00:10:07,027
When he was making  Da'wah(دعوة) to his people in Iraq, only him and Lut(لوط) were the believers.

119
00:10:07,511 --> 00:10:12,019
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى gave Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) a name that wasn't given to anybody else and that is;

120
00:10:12,079 --> 00:10:13,188
 كان أمة

121
00:10:13,408 --> 00:10:15,297
he was nation by himself.

122
00:10:16,177 --> 00:10:18,947
Ibrahim عليه السّلام was a nation, he was an Ummah(امة).

123
00:10:19,914 --> 00:10:25,736
He didn't have anybody with him, he was alone; But Ibrahim عليه السّلام counts as a nation; as a whole Ummah(امة)

124
00:10:26,117 --> 00:10:27,454
 كان أمة

125
00:10:27,744 --> 00:10:30,403
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said: Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) was an Ummah(امة)

126
00:10:31,180 --> 00:10:32,657
and then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said;

127
00:10:32,816 --> 00:10:33,681
Kanitan(كانتًا)

128
00:10:33,943 --> 00:10:40,527
He had a lot of Khushoo(خشوع); he had Khushoo(خشوع) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى in the night and day, 24 hours he was in the state of Khushoo(خشوع).

129
00:10:40,996 --> 00:10:42,186
Kanatan Lillah(كانتًا لله)

130
00:10:42,869 --> 00:10:45,258
and also Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

131
00:10:45,654 --> 00:10:49,336
حَنِيفًا مُسْلِمًا وَمَا كَانَ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ۝

132
00:10:49,386 --> 00:10:52,640
Hanif(حنيف), he stayed away from all Shirk(شرك).

133
00:10:53,489 --> 00:10:57,875
Everyone was trying to pull him to Shirk(شرك); he stayed away from it and that is Hanif(حنيف).

134
00:10:58,137 --> 00:10:59,828
It is Ikhlass Ala Basirah(إخلاص على بصيرة).

135
00:10:59,858 --> 00:11:02,669
He has sincerity and understanding.

136
00:11:04,589 --> 00:11:06,411
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

137
00:11:06,688 --> 00:11:16,100
وَإِذِ ابتَلىٰ إِبراهيمَ رَبُّهُ بِكَلِماتٍ فَأَتَمَّهُنَّ ۖ

138
00:11:16,394 --> 00:11:20,870
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has tested Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) with some commands.

139
00:11:22,259 --> 00:11:23,391
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

140
00:11:23,455 --> 00:11:24,326
 فَأَتَمَّهُنَّ ۖ

141
00:11:24,356 --> 00:11:28,383
He completed them all; He completed them all.

142
00:11:28,622 --> 00:11:30,931
And that's why Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says about about Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم),

143
00:11:30,961 --> 00:11:32,596
وَإِبْرَٰهِيمَ ٱلَّذِى وَفَّىٰٓ

144
00:11:32,771 --> 00:11:39,719
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) has fulfilled; he fulfilled; he fulfilled what Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wanted from him; he fulfilled it all.

145
00:11:40,060 --> 00:11:41,640
وَإِبْرَٰهِيمَ ٱلَّذِى وَفَّىٰٓ

146
00:11:42,187 --> 00:11:45,680
And Allah سبحانه وتعالى says about Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم),

147
00:11:45,887 --> 00:11:51,403
قالَ إِنّي جاعِلُكَ لِلنّاسِ إِمامًا ۖ

148
00:11:51,593 --> 00:11:55,123
I will make you an Imam(اِمَام), a leader for mankind,

149
00:11:55,523 --> 00:11:58,507
someone who will be a role model for everyone to follow.

150
00:11:58,927 --> 00:12:01,213
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says about him;

151
00:12:01,737 --> 00:12:03,848
وَجَعَلْنَا فِي ذُرِّيَّتِهِ النُّبُوَّةَ

152
00:12:04,062 --> 00:12:07,246
We made all of the prophets after him, from his descendants.

153
00:12:08,206 --> 00:12:13,151
All of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and the Rusul(رسل) that came after Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم),

154
